    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.density - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.density.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.density()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate graph density (ratio of actual to possible edges).\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.density()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate graph density (ratio of actual to possible edges).\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.density()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Calculate graph density (ratio of actual to possible edges).\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCalculate graph density (ratio of actual to possible edges).\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L81658-L81723){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.density()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Graph density](../assets/graphs/density.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A five-node graph with four edges drawn solid and the six missing node pairs drawn as faint dashed lines. The result card reads 4 of 10 possible edges, density 0.4.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nDensity measures how complete a graph is. A complete graph has density `1.0`, while a graph\nwith no edges has density `0.0`.\n\nFor directed graphs: `density = E / (N × (N-1))`\nFor undirected graphs: `density = 2E / (N × (N-1))`\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Graph density between `0.0` and `1.0`.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~average_degree`) \n\n:   The mean number of edges per node.\n\n[](`~subgraph`) \n\n:   The graph induced by a set of nodes, to measure the density within it.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA sparse graph with only 2 of the 3 possible edges has a density well below 1:\n\n::: {#91b151dd .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\")])\n\n# 2 edges, 3 nodes: 2 / (3 x 2 / 2) = 0.667\nf\"{graph.density():.3f}\"\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n'0.667'\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nFilling in the missing edge to form a complete graph pushes density up to its maximum,\n`1.0`:\n\n::: {#6ee9eccd .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncomplete = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"A\", \"C\")])\n\nf\"{complete.density():.3f}\"\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n'1.000'\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### A dense city center\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network, with each station in one of three fare\nzones. The 25 stretches of track link only 13% of the 190 pairs of stations, but the\nseven stations of zone 1 are far more tightly linked, with 10 of their 21 pairs:\n\n::: {#f896927a .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\nnodes = metro.get_node_df()\nzone_1 = nodes.filter(nodes[\"zone\"] == 1)[\"id\"].to_list()\n\nround(metro.density(), 2), round(metro.subgraph(zone_1).density(), 2)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(0.13, 0.48)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#e8b8141e .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro.plot(layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"zone\", label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.o